{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z-3=\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-3 & =\\frac{25}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-3 & =5-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-8 & =-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-4(z-8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "509c795bef3ea910e2267c624b53d7889335813a04cef6ac2ad9857f1efad57e"} {"question" "q-35844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbola: $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1$"] ["text" "A parabola: ${y}^{2}=-4(z-8)$"] ["text" "A parabola: ${y}^{2}=4(z-3)$"] ["text" "Two intersecting lines: $y=\\pm 4(x-3)$"] ["text" "Two parallel lines: $y=4(x\\pm 5)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A parabola: ${y}^{2}=-4(z-8)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic paraboloid $z+4=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{4}$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+4 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-4)^{2}}{4} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+4 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=0$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $x$-axis is $(0,0,0)$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "509c795bef3ea910e2267c624b53d7889335813a04cef6ac2ad9857f1efad57e"} {"question" "q-35927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(2,0,0)$"] ["text" "$(-2,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and $(16,0,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(2,0,0)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-35927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,0)$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-73864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z+8={x}^{2}-(y+9)^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-73864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+8 & ={x}^{2}-(y+9)^{2} \\\\ z-(-8) & =\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y-(-9))^{2}}{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(0,-9,-8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-73864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "509c795bef3ea910e2267c624b53d7889335813a04cef6ac2ad9857f1efad57e"} {"question" "q-73864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-73864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,-3,-8)"] ["math" "(0,-3,8)"] ["math" "(0,-9,-8)"] ["math" "(1,-9,-8)"] ["math" "(1,9,8)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-73864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,-9,-8)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-164273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z+4=\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-164273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+4 & =\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ z-(-4) & =\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(3,-1,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de177866c3d5"} {"question" "q-164273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "509c795bef3ea910e2267c624b53d7889335813a04cef6ac2ad9857f1efad57e"} {"question" "q-164273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069167/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ad9d7a8cee85708bdbe44bcce40a958c6dfb67aa0e2c46f6e07de